ms  nobody can predict whether or not there  will be a  you know economic problems the best  thing the government can do is attract  the investment keep people  in work we're doing what we can to help  households i know the chancellor is  looking at further measures that we can  take of course we completely understand  it's a very difficult situation for  people across the country including in  wigan we are facing these global  headwinds and we need to deal with them  by attracting the investment into the  united kingdom making sure that we have  those high quality jobs of course we're  very very concerned about the  circumstances people are facing that's  why we've created things like the  household support fund to help people  get through these difficult times but  ultimately our country's long-term  future is dependent on creating those  high-paid jobs getting that investment  into britain  so how many hours a week should people  have to work in order not to be poor  it's up to people how many uh hours they  work  how many hours they work a week i mean  this is what we are doing is making sure  that all households are supported  through our household support fund it's  not about how many hours people are  working it's about making sure there are  enough of those high paid jobs in the  future  and we're creating at present  lowest unemployment as i've said since  1974 so that we can weather this very  very difficult storm  your home office ministers tell me just  on monday that people should work more  hours than they won't be poor  i think that's a mischaracterization of  what she said okay  we know that it's very very difficult  times for people across the united  kingdom we know that  we are facing higher costs this is a  global phenomenon there's high inflation  across the world because of the energy  price spike  because of the issues with russia  ukraine because of the fact we're  recovering from covered and we want to  do all we can to support households  t